.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "const struct \fBstumpless_error\fP * stumpless_get_error (void)"

.PP
Retrieves the error encountered by the last library call\&. The returned error struct is only valid until the next call to a stumpless function\&. After this, it should not be referred to, and if the error of any subsequent call is needed another call to stumpless_get_error must be made\&.
.PP
Note that the id is the only field of the error that is guaranteed to be set\&. Other members may or may not be set, depending on the context of the error\&.
.PP
If the code_type is NULL, then the code is not valid and should be ignored\&.
.PP
This function does \fInot\fP clear or update the per-thread error code for stumpless, as it is involved in the error handling process itself\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. No synchronization primitives are used as the returned pointer is specific to the thread of execution\&. As a result, the result should not be shared between threads\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&. If you do so, note that if it is called before a stumpless library function in the handler itself the result will not be meaningful\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A \fBstumpless_error\fP struct describing the error encountered by the last function call\&. If no error was encountered, this will be NULL\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "enum \fBstumpless_error_id\fP stumpless_get_error_id (const struct \fBstumpless_error\fP * err)"

.PP
Gets the error id of the given error\&. \fBThread Safety: MT-Safe race:err\fP This function is thread safe, as long as err is not modifed by other threads during this call\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be asynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBSince\fP
.RS 4
release v1\&.5\&.0
.RE
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIerr\fP The error to get the id from\&. This must not be NULL\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The error id of the given error\&. 
.RE
.PP

