.SS "void stumpless_set_error_stream (FILE * stream)"

.PP
Sets the stream to write errors to\&. This will be stderr by default, but can be set to any stream\&. If it is set to NULL then error messages will not be printed (essentially skipping all \fCstumpless_perror\fP calls)\&.
.PP
\fBThread Safety: MT-Safe\fP This function is thread safe\&. Atomic variables are used to store and retrieve the error stream\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Signal Safety: AS-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from signal handlers\&.
.PP
\fBAsync Cancel Safety: AC-Safe\fP This function is safe to call from threads that may be ansynchronously cancelled\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIstream\fP The stream to write errors to\&. If this is NULL then the messages intended for the error stream will be ignored\&. 
.RE
.PP

